 * Hand-written because neither `Json` flag covers this case, which is easy to assume otherwise:
 * `ignoreUnknownKeys` forgives an unknown *key* and says nothing about an unknown enum *value*, and
 * `coerceInputValues` only rescues a property that declares a default — [FinishIssue.field] has
 * none, and giving it one would silently invent an issue kind for a *missing* field too, not just
 * an unrecognised one. Without this, a single unrecognised value fails the whole readiness response
 * and takes every issue the client *does* understand down with it.
 *
 * Encoding is the plain member name for symmetry only. Nothing in this client sends a
 * [FinishIssueField] — readiness is a response — so [FinishIssueField.UNKNOWN] is never put on the
 * wire; if some future request ever carries one, it needs a decision of its own here rather than
 * this fallthrough.
 */
